      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "CH'ÊN Yüan-pin 陳元贇 (T. 義都, H. 既白山人, 菊秀軒, 升庵, 芝山) 1587–1671, was a native of Hangchow, Chekiang. In the spring of 1621 he accompanied Shan Fêng-hsiang 單鳳翔, an official of Chekiang, on a journey to Japan to lodge a protest against piratical activities along the China coast.",
